{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.JHopfQOneProvenance","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.JHopfQOneProvenance","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.JonesNuclearQuotient"],"declarations":10,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.JHopfQOneProvenance.jonesHopf_provenance","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.JHopfQOneProvenance.jonesHopf_provenance","kind":"theorem","line":116,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/JHopfQOneProvenance.lean#L116-L119","doc":"**The two routes agree at `t = 1`.** The tabulated closed form and the\n`(−2)^{c−1}` loop-factor value both give `−2` for the Hopf link. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.JHopfQOneProvenance.jonesHopfStd_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.JHopfQOneProvenance.jonesHopfStd_one","kind":"theorem","line":111,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/JHopfQOneProvenance.lean#L111-L114","doc":"**`V_Hopf(1) = −2`** from the tabulated closed form — cross-checks the\n`(−2)^{c−1}` route (`jonesHopf_atOne`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.JHopfQOneProvenance.jonesHopfStd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.JHopfQOneProvenance.jonesHopfStd","kind":"def","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/JHopfQOneProvenance.lean#L106-L109","doc":"**Tabulated standard normalized Jones polynomial of the (negative) Hopf\nlink** `V(t) = −t^{1/2} − t^{5/2}` (Jones 1987; standard link tables), in\n`√q` form (`(√q)^5 = q^{5/2}`). Independent of the loop-factor route. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.JHopfQOneProvenance.unknot_atOne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.JHopfQOneProvenance.unknot_atOne","kind":"theorem","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/JHopfQOneProvenance.lean#L101-L104","doc":"The unknot (`c = 1`) gives `(−2)^0 = 1` — consistent with the framework's\nnormalization `V_unknot(1) = 1` in the V-convention. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.JHopfQOneProvenance.jonesHopf_atOne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.JHopfQOneProvenance.jonesHopf_atOne","kind":"theorem","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/JHopfQOneProvenance.lean#L95-L99","doc":"**`J_Hopf(q=1) = −2`.** The Hopf link has `c = 2` components, so\n`classicalJonesAtOne 2 = (−2)^{2−1} = −2`. This is the provenance of the\n`c_3` near-match constant. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.JHopfQOneProvenance.classicalJonesAtOne_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.JHopfQOneProvenance.classicalJonesAtOne_eq","kind":"theorem","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/JHopfQOneProvenance.lean#L91-L93","doc":"`classicalJonesAtOne c = (−2)^{c−1}` — the classical `V_L(1) = (−2)^{c−1}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.JHopfQOneProvenance.classicalJonesAtOne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.JHopfQOneProvenance.classicalJonesAtOne","kind":"def","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/JHopfQOneProvenance.lean#L86-L89","doc":"**The classical Jones value at `t = 1` for a `c`-component link**, as the\n`(c−1)`-th power of the loop factor `δ(1)`. This is the QOU-side statement of\nthe classical identity `V_L(1) = (−2)^{c−1}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.JHopfQOneProvenance.jonesHopfLink_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.JHopfQOneProvenance.jonesHopfLink_one","kind":"theorem","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/JHopfQOneProvenance.lean#L76-L84","doc":"**The framework's reduced Markov trace of the Hopf closure is `1` at `q=1`,\nNOT `−2`.** Makes the convention gap explicit: `h(1) = 0` kills the\ntrace-dependent term, leaving the reduced-trace normalization `1`. The `−2`\nis therefore *not* the raw reduced trace but the loop-factor / V-normalized\nvalue. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.JHopfQOneProvenance.loopValue_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.JHopfQOneProvenance.loopValue_one","kind":"theorem","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/JHopfQOneProvenance.lean#L71-L74","doc":"**`δ(1) = −2`.** The entire `J_Hopf(q=1) = −2` originates here: the loop\nfactor at the classical point `t = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.JHopfQOneProvenance.loopValue","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.JHopfQOneProvenance.loopValue","kind":"def","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/JHopfQOneProvenance.lean#L66-L69","doc":"**The Jones loop factor** `δ(q) = −(√q + 1/√q)` — the value of a single\nunknotted loop, and the base of the `(δ)^{n−1}` prefactor in Jones's\nnormalization of the Markov trace. ","signatureChunk":0}]}